  "reviewNotes": [
    "Dictionary headwords and explicit grouped spelling variants were read in the original PDF. Printed page numbers, rather than PDF page indices, are recorded.",
    "Alaudala is treated under Alaudula as an explicitly amended form. Paragallinula postdates the dictionary and uses the original authors' etymology on printed page 6.",
    "Person names are species-specific: Ardeola grayii honours John Edward Gray; Bucorvus leadbeateri Benjamin Leadbeater; Anarhynchus wilsonia Alexander Wilson.",
    "Perisoreus retains the dictionary's unresolved origin and competing suggestions. Examinandus explicitly preserves the dictionary's shift to examinatus rather than silently presenting that different spelling as a certain derivation.",
    "All existing 940 generated species rows and term explanations must remain unchanged.",
    "The concept-verified 2026 House Bunting combination Fringillaria sahari uses the separate Fringillaria entry on p.164, never the Emberiza provenance on p.145.",
    "The Museum Heineanum collection account explicitly identifies the Volga lark type Calandritis Heinei Homeyer, 1873 as named for Ferdinand Heine senior (PDF page 19). This supplies taxon-specific dedication evidence in addition to the dictionary's general heinei entry.",
    "For Perisoreus, the dictionary labels an alternative intensifier peri as Latin. The gloss does not repeat that doubtful language attribution; it describes the older proposal as an unspecified intensifying prefix with Latin sorix, while preserving the uncertainty of the entire etymology."
  ],
